1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Thom: We can still fix this, Celia. Give me one more minute before you walk off the bridge.

2
00:00:40,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Celia: You promised you wouldn't let the rocket project come between us, Thom. My robotic hand is proof enough.

3
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Forty years later inside the reinforced Oude Kerk laboratory in Amsterdam, Barley calibrates the holographic neural projector.

4
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Barley: The cyborg army outside the dome is tearing through the perimeter shields. We only have one shot at rewriting her memory.

5
00:02:44,000 --> 00:03:18,000
An older Thom steps onto the wooden recreation of the canal bridge while robotic arms project Celia's likeness into the chamber.

6
00:03:30,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Thom: Celia, wait. Tell me what really drove you away from the launch pad that night.

7
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Celia's neural avatar flickers as automated sniper drones breach the stained-glass dome high above the lab.

8
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Barley yells from the console as explosive plasma bolts shatter the scaffolding around the memory rig.

9
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Thom reaches out and accepts Celia's anger instead of erasing it, stabilizing the core memory signal.

10
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:45,000
The cyborg Celia lowers her weapon outside the shattered church doors as dawn breaks over Amsterdam.
